---
/**
 * Replaces Starlight's light/dark theme provider.
 *
 * Starlight's stock version reads localStorage and `prefers-color-scheme` and
 * stamps `data-theme` on <html> before paint. Every themed component keys off
 * that attribute — Starlight's own colour variables, but also Expressive Code,
 * which swaps its syntax theme independently. Pinning only the CSS variables
 * left code blocks following the OS, so the attribute itself has to be fixed.
 *
 * The landing page declares `color-scheme: light` and has no dark palette, so
 * the docs commit to light too rather than handing a dark-preferring reader a
 * cream landing page followed by a dark docs site.
 *
 * Setting it in the markup means it is already correct in the served HTML;
 * there is no flash, and no script is needed to sustain it.
 */
---

<script is:inline>
  // Starlight's client-side navigation and view transitions can re-run theme
  // logic; keep the attribute pinned rather than assuming the static value
  // survives. Cheap, idempotent, and no-ops when already correct.
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "light";
</script>
